<title>USA: Midwest Cash Grain PM - Soybean basis values rise.</title>
<headline>Midwest Cash Grain PM - Soybean basis values rise.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-05-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean basis bids rose three to four cents per bushel at river markets late Friday in reaction to a three-cent gain in nearby CIF basis bids to 29 over CBOT July at the U.S. Gulf, grain dealers said.</p>
<p>The higher basis bids failed to produce a large amount of country movement. Export sources said the Gulf values rose to be competitive with strong processor bids.</p>
<p>&quot;I think the processors are taking all the beans, plus a few boats are coming in the first of June,&quot; said an exporter.</p>
<p>Corn and wheat basis values were mostly unchanged in light activity.</p>
<p>Some rail corn basis offers may be adjusted downward next week in reaction to expected lowering of some rail freight rates, a few Midwest dealers said.  </p>
<p>Basis values are quoted against CBOT futures, cash $/bu.</p>
